input arrays reversed: sec 7.4: a stranger's record of the handing off's second carries succession-shaped bytes the old key signed at seq 1 that fail sec 4.3 (no `to`): they set no retiring seq, which stays 3, so the old key's entry at seq 2 carried in that second counts and the succession at 3 admits its key; the stranger's record is DISCARDED and its bytes MALFORMED; COMPLETE with five entries.
